{"entries":[{"caption":"Appendix D — The water-peak filter in detail","key":"sec-glandular-details","order":{"number":1,"section":[4,0,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Left: the share of patients whose first-named breast has the higher Water:Fat, using every scan (grey) and using only the scans the rule accepts, with both breasts usable (blue), with the number of patients and the two-sided binomial p-value against 50%. Right: the CANCER vs NORMAL result for water peak thresholds from 0 to 0.6 (the water centre rule unchanged), with the patients compared written at every 0.1; the grey line is every scan and the dashed line the chosen threshold.","key":"fig-on-the-fly","order":{"number":1,"section":[4,1,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Patients the rule compares (blue) and leaves out (grey). Left: BI-RADS breast density, the category the radiology reports mention most often for each patient. Right: age, where the sheets give it; one dot per patient.","key":"fig-who-left-out","order":{"number":6,"section":[4,5,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Rejected scans. As Figure fig-usable-by-age, but each breast is the mean of the scans the test rejects.","key":"fig-rejected-by-age","order":{"number":4,"section":[4,3,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Each patient’s two breasts compared, using only the usable scans (blue) or only the rejected scans (grey); one dot per patient. Left: the signed difference, first-named − second (CANCER − NORMAL, etc.; NORMAL vs NORMAL is LEFT − RIGHT); above 0, the first-named breast has more water. Right: |A − B|, which does not need to know which breast is which. Boxes span the middle half of the patients, the thick line is the median, and the whiskers reach the furthest patient within 1.5 box-lengths.","key":"fig-differences","order":{"number":2,"section":[4,2,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Usable scans. Mean prepared curve of NORMAL, BENIGN and CANCER breasts, one panel per age band (each breast is the mean of its usable scans), with ±1 SD across breasts shaded. The dashed line is the usable-scan water threshold over q 20–22.","key":"fig-usable-by-age","order":{"number":3,"section":[4,3,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Usable and rejected scans by age","key":"sec-usable-and-rejected-scans-by-age","order":{"number":1,"section":[4,3,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"All usable breasts: water peak height (mean over q 20–22 of the breast’s usable-scan mean) against patient age. Points coloured by label; solid line is ordinary least squares within that label; dashed line is the usable-scan water threshold.","key":"fig-usable-normal","order":{"number":5,"section":[4,4,0,0,0,0,0]}}],"headings":["every-scan-against-usable-scans-and-the-threshold","how-different-the-two-breasts-are","sec-usable-and-rejected-scans-by-age","water-peak-against-age","who-the-rule-leaves-out","is-it-just-the-odds-of-hitting-glandular-tissue","sec-glandular-details"],"options":{"chapter-id":"sec-glandular-details","chapters":true,"chapters-alpha":true,"chapters-appendix":true}}